WebSocket/Server-Sent Events - Real-time emergency alerts from backend to UI
Audio API - Emergency alarm playback

Network Communication Protocol

Listening Port: UDP/TCP port (e.g., 5000) for incoming emergency packets
Packet Format: JSON structure containing:

Elevator ID/MAC address
Building identifier
Floor number
Timestamp
Emergency status (pressed/acknowledged)
Optional: additional sensor data



Core Features
1. Dashboard Builder (Configuration Mode)

Drag-and-drop interface for positioning elevator icons on a visual canvas
Elevator properties panel for configuring:

Unique elevator ID (matches network node)
Building name
Floor number
Physical location description
IP address or MAC address of elevator node


Grid/canvas system representing physical site layout
Save/load configuration to persistent storage
Visual grouping by building or zone

2. Real-Time Monitoring Mode

Live status display of all configured elevators
Color-coded indicators:

Green: Normal operation
Red: Emergency active
Gray: Offline/no communication


Last contact timestamp for each elevator
Automatic layout based on saved dashboard configuration

3. Emergency Alert System

Immediate visual alert:

Full-screen or prominent modal popup
Flashing red border/background
Large text showing building, floor, and elevator ID
Timestamp of emergency activation


Audible alarm:

Continuous or pulsing emergency sound
Adjustable volume
Continues until acknowledged


Alert queue for multiple simultaneous emergencies
Alert history log with timestamps

4. Acknowledgment Mechanism

Deliberate user action required:

Large "ACKNOWLEDGE EMERGENCY" button
Optional: require typing elevator ID for confirmation
Optional: add operator notes/comments


Network response:

Send acknowledgment packet back to originating elevator node
Include timestamp and operator ID (if applicable)


Status update:

Stop alarm sound
Update elevator status on dashboard
Log acknowledgment event



5. Data Logging and History

SQLite database storing:

Emergency event records (timestamp, elevator, duration, acknowledger)
System health logs (elevator connectivity, packet statistics)
Configuration changes
Operator actions


Export functionality for reports (CSV/PDF)
Search and filter historical events

6. System Health Monitoring

Watchdog timers for each elevator (detect offline nodes)
Network statistics (packets received, latency)
System resource monitoring (CPU, memory, network usage)
Auto-reconnection logic for dropped connections

